# Cursor Rules for BlameBackend

Refer to AGENTS.md at the repository root for the full specification and rules.

Key Invariants:
1. Zero-Semantics Alteration: Never modify intercepted HTTP request or response bodies. Use `response.peekBody(maxBytes)` in OkHttp or clone/save channels in Ktor.
2. Catch, Log & Re-throw: Always catch network exceptions, dispatch telemetry to `InspectorEventBus`, and immediately re-throw (`throw e`).
3. Defensive Redaction: Mask `Authorization`, `Cookie`, `Set-Cookie`, `x-api-key`, and other tokens using case-insensitive checks.
4. Fail-Soft Transport: An unreachable daemon or socket error must never crash the target mobile/desktop app.
5. Strict KMP Boundaries: Keep `commonMain` pure; never import `java.io.*` or Android classes in `commonMain`.
6. Enforce 64 KB Payload Cap: Set `truncated: true` when exceeding 64 KB.
7. Sanitize Shell Arguments: Validate device serial IDs with `/^[a-zA-Z0-9.:_-]+$/` before calling ADB.
